body:
I have a flake that I'm trying to use with nix-direnv and nix-ld to set up my development environment, however NIX_LD_LIBRARY_PATH seems to not work while LD_LIBRARY_PATH does. I am using nix-ld from nixpkgs-unstable on NixOS. My flake:
```
{
  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixpkgs-unstable";
    
    rust-overlay = {
      url = "github:oxalica/rust-overlay";
      inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
    };
  };
  
  outputs = inputs: let
    system = "x86_64-linux";
    overlays = [ (import inputs.rust-overlay) ];
    pkgs = import inputs.nixpkgs {
      inherit system overlays;
    };
  in {
    devShells.${system}.default = pkgs.mkShell rec {
      nativeBuildInputs = with pkgs; [
        pkg-config
        
        (rust-bin.stable.latest.default.override {
          extensions = [
            "rust-analyzer"
            "rust-src"
          ];
        })
      ];
      buildInputs = with pkgs; [
        udev alsa-lib vulkan-loader
        xorg.libX11 xorg.libXcursor xorg.libXi xorg.libXrandr # To use the x11 feature
        libxkbcommon wayland # To use the wayland feature
      ];
      NIX_LD_LIBRARY_PATH = pkgs.lib.makeLibraryPath buildInputs;
      WINIT_UNIX_BACKEND = "wayland";
      # RUST_SRC_PATH = "${rust-bin-pkg}/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library";
    };
  };
}
```

I am trying to use Platformio. How ever it uses unpatched  binaries when compiling code. 
I then setup a develop environment using flakes and nix-ld.
```nix
{
  description = "A basic flake with a shell";
  inputs.nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-24.05";
  inputs.flake-utils.url = "github:numtide/flake-utils";
  inputs.nix-ld.url = "github:Mic92/nix-ld";
  # this line assume that you also have nixpkgs as an input
  inputs.nix-ld.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";

  outputs = { nixpkgs, flake-utils, nix-ld, ... }:
    flake-utils.lib.eachDefaultSystem (system:
      let
        pkgs = nixpkgs.legacyPackages.${system};
        # buildInputs = with pkgs; [  ];
      in with pkgs; {
        programs.nix-ld.enable = true;
        devShells.default = mkShell {
          packages = with pkgs; [ gcc zlib stdenv.cc.cc.lib platformio-core ];
          NIX_LD_LIBRARY_PATH =
            lib.makeLibraryPath [ pkgs.stdenv.cc.cc.lib openssl gcc ];
          NIX_LD = lib.fileContents "${stdenv.cc}/nix-support/dynamic-linker";
          # inherit buildInputs;

          shellHook = ''
            export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$NIX_LD_LIBRARY_PATH
            export PLATFORMIO_CORE_DIR=$(pwd)/.platformio
            echo Hi
          '';
        };
      });
}
```
I then enter the shell by running `nix develop --impure -c $SHELL`.

When I look at the binary with `ldd` I get the output
```shell
ldd .platformio/packages/toolchain-xtensa-esp32s3/bin/xtensa-esp32s3-elf-g++
	linux-vdso.so.1 (0x00007ffff7fc6000)
	libstdc++.so.6 => /nix/store/qksd2mz9f5iasbsh398akdb58fx9kx6d-gcc-13.2.0-lib/lib/libstdc++.so.6 (0x00007ffff7c00000)
	libm.so.6 => /nix/store/r8qsxm85rlxzdac7988psm7gimg4dl3q-glibc-2.39-52/lib/libm.so.6 (0x00007ffff7edd000)
	libc.so.6 => /nix/store/r8qsxm85rlxzdac7988psm7gimg4dl3q-glibc-2.39-52/lib/libc.so.6 (0x00007ffff7a13000)
	/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 => /nix/store/r8qsxm85rlxzdac7988psm7gimg4dl3q-glibc-2.39-52/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 (0x00007ffff7fc8000)
	libgcc_s.so.1 => /nix/store/qksd2mz9f5iasbsh398akdb58fx9kx6d-gcc-13.2.0-lib/lib/libgcc_s.so.1 (0x00007ffff7eb8000)
```
I think this means that it has all dependents.  
However, when I try to run the binary I still get the generic NixOS error message:
```shell
Could not start dynamically linked executable: .platformio/packages/toolchain-xtensa-esp32s3/bin/xtensa-esp32s3-elf-g++
NixOS cannot run dynamically linked executables intended for generic
linux environments out of the box. For more information, see:
https://nix.dev/permalink/stub-ld
```
How do I activate nix-ld so I can run this binary?

[nushell](https://www.nushell.sh/)is a modern terminal written in Rust.

When the user enables nushell, the Node for VSCode Remote cannot start. However, VSCode Remote's Node can start when the user enables zsh.

```
users.users."root" = {
  shell = pkgs.nushell;
};
```

```
cannot execute /root/.vscode-server/bin/6c3e3dba23e8fadc360aed75ce363ba185c497944/node
You are trying to run an unpatched binary on nixos, but you have not configured NIX_LD or NIX_LD_x86_64-linux. See https://github.com/Mic92/nix-ld for more details
```

I think it may be due to environment variables.

Following the Nix flake instructions, I get

```
$ nixos-rebuild build --flake path:.
error: access to canonical path '/nix/store/55ayck4pllh4qallb1dbhbkrzwrrl02r-binutils-wrapper-2.35.2/nix-support/dynamic-linker' is forbidden in restricted mode
```

